{"text":"abdominal pain","id":"D015746","label":"Disease"},{"text":"toxicity","id":"D064420","label":"Disease"}],"head":"ioxaglate","head_id":"D007485","pairs":[{"head":"diatrizoate","tail":"nausea","head_id":"D003973","tail_id":"D009325"},{"head":"diatrizoate","tail":"dizziness","head_id":"D003973","tail_id":"D004244"},{"head":"diatrizoate","tail":"abdominal pain","head_id":"D003973","tail_id":"D015746"},{"head":"diatrizoate","tail":"toxicity","head_id":"D003973","tail_id":"D064420"},{"head":"acetrizoate","tail":"nausea","head_id":"D000100","tail_id":"D009325"},{"head":"acetrizoate","tail":"dizziness","head_id":"D000100","tail_id":"D004244"},{"head":"acetrizoate","tail":"abdominal pain","head_id":"D000100","tail_id":"D015746"},{"head":"acetrizoate","tail":"toxicity","head_id":"D000100","tail_id":"D064420"},{"head":"iocarmate","tail":"nausea","head_id":"C025504","tail_id":"D009325"},{"head":"iocarmate","tail":"dizziness","head_id":"C025504","tail_id":"D004244"},{"head":"iocarmate","tail":"abdominal pain","head_id":"C025504","tail_id":"D015746"},{"head":"iocarmate","tail":"toxicity","head_id":"C025504","tail_id":"D064420"},{"head":"ioxaglate","tail":"nausea","head_id":"D007485","tail_id":"D009325"},{"head":"ioxaglate","tail":"dizziness","head_id":"D007485","tail_id":"D004244"},{"head":"ioxaglate","tail":"abdominal pain","head_id":"D007485","tail_id":"D015746"},{"head":"ioxaglate","tail":"toxicity","head_id":"D007485","tail_id":"D064420"}],"relations":["D003973 | D009325","D003973 | D004244","D003973 | D015746","D003973 | D064420","D000100 | D009325","D000100 | D004244","D000100 | D015746","D000100 | D064420","C025504 | D009325","C025504 | D004244","C025504 | D015746","C025504 | D064420","D007485 | D009325","D007485 | D004244","D007485 | D064420"],"result":"$","tail":"toxicity","tail_id":"D064420","text":"Comparative study: Endografine (diatrizoate), Vasurix polyvidone (acetrizoate), Dimer-X (iocarmate) and Hexabrix (ioxaglate) in hysterosalpingography. Side effects of hysterosalpingography with Dimer-X, Hexabrix, Vasurix polyvidone and Endografine in 142 consecutive patients, receiving one of the four tested media were evaluated from replies to postal questionnaires. The Dimer-X group had a higher incidence of nausea and dizziness. The Endografine group had a higher incidence of abdominal pain. These differences occur especially in the age groups under 30 years. Hexabrix and Vasurix polyvidone are considered the best contrast media for hysterosalpingography and perhaps because of its low toxicity Hexabrix should be preferred.","metrics":{"precision":0.13333333333333333,"recall":0.6666666666666666,"f1":0.2222222222222222,"rel_tp":2,"rel_fp":13,"rel_fn":1}}